envelope: 1
uuid: nexus-export-schema-response
type: schema
id: response
context: >-
  guardian/schemas — sovereign local copy. Origin: lib/node-schemas/schema.response (shared
  canonical version, may have moved on independently since this copy was made — sovereignty means
  guardian does not depend on it at runtime, not that the two can never drift).
intent: null
summary: null
system: guardian
tags: []
exported_at: 1789330000100
source: nexus.lib.node-export
payload:
  status: REAL
  source: >-
    §MCO16e 2026-09-13 — guardian is a real, direct writer of this type: POST /dom/event
    (guardian/server.js) persists a real .response node for every live DOM mutation event it
    receives, via lib/component-ledger.js's write() plus lib/node-export.js's exportToFile().
  fields:
    uuid:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real, unique id for this response event
    compartmentUuid:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: >-
        the real, live compartment this response belongs to — dropped, not fabricated, when absent.
        §MCO16f 2026-09-14 — relaxed from required:true when jobId was added: a job-origin DOM
        event genuinely has no compartment, and node-schemas.js's checkPayload() cannot express
        "one of these two" (see NODE-TAXONOMY.md's own "Still mechanically open" note). The real
        constraint is enforced in guardian/lib/response-nodes.js's writeResponseNode().
    queueId:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: the real RAID queue row this compartment is executing, when one exists
    jobId:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: >-
        §MCO16f 2026-09-14 — the real guardian job this DOM event belongs to, when the event came
        from a job rather than a compartment. Added because guardian/lib/response-nodes.js is a
        real second writer with a real second origin (userscript startWatch, which has a jobId and
        no compartment). See that module's own §HONEST SCHEMA NOTE for why the real "at least one
        of compartmentUuid/jobId" rule is enforced in the writer and not here.
    sequence:
      type: number
      required: false
      description: >-
        monotonic index of this event within one job/compartment — real ordering that survives
        equal-millisecond timestamps, which a live MutationObserver genuinely produces
    phase:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: reserved — currently carried in domEventType; kept out of use until a real second axis exists
    domEventType:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: 'the real event kind — e.g. dom.mutation, dom.snapshot, dom.ready'
    agentId:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: which real agent/provider produced this event, when known
    payload:
      type: object
      required: false
      description: the real, event-specific data
    ts:
      type: number
      required: true
      description: real event timestamp — logical ordering axis
